course: dictionary
lesson: 4377
title: Habit in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A habit is something you do often and regularly, often without thinking about it. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The bathroom has its own good habits: your own toothbrush, the toilet lid down, hot hair tools switched off and the fan on after a steamy bath.» These are things people do again and again, so a habit is something you repeat.
explain: A good habit helps you, like brushing your teeth. A bad habit harms you or annoys others, like biting your nails. «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» The words good and bad tell you which kind of habit each one is.
explain: Look for clues that a habit is being made. Doing something every day, or doing it without thinking, are signs of a habit. Try the check: swap in "something you always do" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A habit is something you do often and regularly, often without thinking about it.
fact: A good habit helps you; a bad habit harms you or annoys others.
fact: Repeating something every day turns it into a habit, and a habit takes time to make or to break.
fact: «Break a habit» means stop doing it; «get into the habit of» means start doing something regularly.
fact: A habit can also be the long robe worn by a nun or a monk.
exercise: «Virtues are good habits such as honesty and courage; vices are bad habits such as greed and cruelty.» What is a vice? | * A bad habit, such as greed | A long robe worn by a monk | A good habit, such as honesty | Something you do only once
exercise: Which of these is a bad habit? | Getting enough sleep | Eating vegetables | *Biting your nails | Brushing your teeth twice a day
exercise: What turns something into a habit? | * Repeating it every day | Doing it only once | Forgetting it quickly | Asking a friend about it
test: «The bathroom has its own good habits: your own toothbrush, the toilet lid down, hot hair tools switched off and the fan on after a steamy bath.» What does habit mean in this sentence? | * Something you do often and regularly | Something you do only once | A bad mood that lasts all day | A long robe worn by a monk
test: Which phrase means start doing something regularly? | Pick a habit | Break a habit | * Get into the habit of | Bite your nails
exam: Which word means done as a habit, usual? | habitat | * habitual | hobby | hurry
